Package: DSEMr
Title: Bayesian Dynamic Structural Equation Modeling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcus", "Harris", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"),
    person("The extendr contributors", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Authors of vendored Rust crates; see inst/AUTHORS")
  )
Description: Specifies, simulates, and estimates Bayesian dynamic structural
    equation models for intensive longitudinal and time-series data using a
    compiled 'Rust' numerical backend and an R reference engine. Models can be
    expressed with an extension of 'lavaan' syntax or a clean-room 'Mplus'
    Version 9 compatibility language and compile to a unified intermediate
    representation. Supports single-level vector autoregressive, residual
    dynamic (Asparouhov and Muthen, 2020, <doi:10.1080/10705511.2019.1626733>),
    dynamic factor, white-noise factor score, and binary or ordinal probit
    models; two-level location-scale dynamic models with latent centering,
    random slopes, random log innovation variances, and between-level
    structural regressions (Asparouhov, Hamaker, and Muthen, 2018,
    <doi:10.1080/10705511.2017.1406803>; McNeish and Hamaker, 2020,
    <doi:10.1037/met0000250>); three-level dynamic structural equation models
    with three-level latent variable decomposition; cross-classified subject-by-time
    models; time-interval grid alignment; penalized shrinkage priors; within-cluster
    standardized estimates (Schuurman, Ferrer, de Boer-Sonnenschein, and
    Hamaker, 2016, <doi:10.1037/met0000062>); covariate variance inflation
    factors; and deterministic parallel Monte Carlo simulation studies.
